not meeting integral constraint: objective(y) + penalty*((integral(y) - 1)/dx)**2  \n- Reparamterization: use the mean squared error between the intended score and the current one as the objective.  \n\n### 5. Compute Budget and Robustness  \nFor n=560:  \n- Each evaluation of the objective requires integer operations of order O(560).  \n- We hope to execute 100-150 outer loops (m=60..100) and for each 2-5 inner optimizations (costly).  \n\nUse multiprocessing (if available) to run multiple trials in parallel.  \n\nIf optimization fails, fall back to the parent solution.  \n\n### 6. Validation and Return Contract  \n- Ensure the candidate satisfies 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and sum(h)=n/2.  \n- Check for NaN/Inf in objective.  \n- Use the same overlap evaluator as the parent program.  \n- Return with the best candidate found and score.  \n\nNote: This is an evolved strategy designed to improve on the record by leveraging combinatorial optimization of interval-based solutions, avoiding the fruitless exploration of the continuous high-dimensional space. The code will be implemented by the developer accordingly.",
